The current original-development corpus is `original-corpus-v3/corpus.json`
(SHA-256 `d1d9171feab96665d0b3a4eb72b0c929414e6a37493475d203544fe0326a7299`).
Its four families, six-event source/configuration sequence, four arms, cold/warm
profiles and seven one-factor controls remain unchanged. It is a concrete
public-input corpus and source-transport qualification, not a dispatch freeze
or a completed integrated evaluation.

Two explicit authority corrections precede this version. The curator's
`original_acceptance_v1/public_contract_v3/objectives.json` replaces the newly
authored OAuth combined-server exact response-key assertion with the qualified
well-formed successful-metadata contract. All original visible/private criteria
remain unchanged. The old contract, its 3/4 reference outcome and the separate
supplemental candidate's hidden-check failure remain retained. The corrected
OAuth objective record is `d5045381be97c93d1c30c58fb6738f33177a76556f58fe5c21c569b8f1dc162c`;
its text is `a4094e26bdf9338d7f5661d2d2b6b13979efe769dd372c324aaf54cbf469ff7f`.
XML, Pyparsing and Click objective identities did not change.

The original source-cache checkout modes also differed from the authoritative
historical archive reconstruction: 0664/0775 versus 0644/0755. Every file's bytes
and the one Pyparsing symlink were already identical. The mismatch is retained
in `original-inventory-projection-v1/observation.json`; it was detected before
candidate dispatch. The curator's separately materialized `public_bases_v1`
restores archive modes and leaves the earlier roots unchanged. Corpus v3 binds
that admission (`e53b8f11af5559462c918835ecc586b9a04dd48377a74b6315ade13ee1dcbcf2`)
and independently checks unchanged content/population and all four exact
original-adapter inventory hashes. Its `preserve_base_modes` transport now
starts from those authoritative bases.

| Qualification against corpus v3 | Result |
| --- | --- |
| `generic-transport-controls-v3/summary.json` | 144 passing source/patch/mode/Git/retrieval controls over eight public bases; 18.086047 seconds. |
| `original-source-branch-controls-v2/summary.json` | 323 passing controls and 72 full source/configuration transitions. Declared fixture acceptance flags are not behavioral outcomes. |
| `generic_transport_admission_v2.json` | 283 read-only joins of source snapshots, complete inventories, patches, configurations and declared fixture records. |
| `original-message-controls-v1/summary.json` | 296 passing controls; all 72 initial generic requests fit three modules, 48,000 raw source bytes and 65,536 serialized wire bytes. Largest measured wire: 56,757 bytes. |

The generic residual message helper is `original_messages_v1.py`. It admits
the public repair surface as mandatory initial source, exposes the same complete
public module catalog to every arm, and retains exact raw fallback prompt
identity across A–D. It separately binds the public objective record/text and
API configuration. Scorer logs, reference fields, hidden case names and arbitrary
strings inside purported count fields do not enter the model prompt; a retained
sentinel control verifies the projection across current checks, history and
feedback. Source expansions and growing retry feedback still require an exact
wire check immediately before every eventual dispatch. These are offline
request measurements; no model telemetry or savings estimate follows.

All controls above made zero provider/scorer calls. Prior corpora, qualification
runs, the original inventory discrepancy and both Requests cohorts remain
unchanged. The version-2 validation-action procedure service is now qualified
for current-scorer nomination only. Nomination is not scoring success or
permission to skip a whole grader. The six-event caller's closed nomination
request is checked in
`original-caller-nomination-controls-v1/summary.json` (24 admitted
constructions, 60 checks, zero native/scorer/provider executions). Actual
CALL-phase reuse still needs its own source/environment/fixture/certificate
controls, with setup and teardown preserved. Provider-disabled XML cold A and D executions now exist in
`original-xml-a-cold-offline-v1/` and `original-xml-d-cold-offline-v2/`. Native
publication/recovery bindings, CALL reuse, the remaining families and the final
effect/call/source freeze remain required before any live original-development
cohort.
